<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n85489" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολύ-φημος</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολύ-φᾱμος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>abounding in songs and legends,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀοιδός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					22.376
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολύφατος, θρῆνος
				πολύφαμος</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>I.</u>
				8(7).64
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>manyvoiced, wordy,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγορὴν πολύφημον ἱκέσθην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					2.150
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐς πολύφημον ἐξενεῖκαι</span>
			to bring it forth to <i>the many-voiced,</i> i.e. <i>the agora
				(the 'parliament'),</i> Orac. ap. <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				5.79
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>much spoken of, famous,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁδός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Parm.
					1.2
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ π. καὶ πολυώνυμος σοφός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					1.371
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
